WEBVTT

00:00:09,070 --> 00:00:18,070
I get a burning sensation sometimes where I had radiation in the past after my left breast mastectomy nearly four years ago.

00:00:18,070 --> 00:00:23,070
What would be the causes of this and what could I do to prevent it?

00:00:23,070 --> 00:00:30,070
So a burning sensation anywhere in your body can be a side of something going on.

00:00:30,070 --> 00:00:37,070
So that can be cells reproducing to heal the area.

00:00:37,070 --> 00:00:44,070
If it's where you had post surgery, where you had radiation, it's a concern.

00:00:44,070 --> 00:00:52,070
Of course, it is because you can get cancer coming back at an area where you had cancer before.

00:00:52,070 --> 00:00:57,070
Certainly you could get a totally different type of cancer where you had radiation.

00:00:57,070 --> 00:01:00,070
That's what I don't like about soft tissue radiation.

00:01:00,070 --> 00:01:12,070
There's plenty of data that shows the higher incidence of melanomas where there was radiation for breast cancer or other cancers.

00:01:12,070 --> 00:01:17,070
So yeah, it's a concern.

00:01:17,070 --> 00:01:27,070
It's something that if you're still getting regular checkups with an oncologist getting a PET scan might be appropriate.

00:01:27,070 --> 00:01:37,070
Can be just the tissue healing can be just scar formation too, so I don't want to raise too much concern when it's not necessary.

00:01:37,070 --> 00:01:43,070
But it's something to be aware of.

00:01:43,070 --> 00:01:50,070
Certainly, when you have scar formation from an injury in the past, you can get that type of feeling.

00:01:50,070 --> 00:02:00,070
Even if it's like you cut yourself really bad, you had stitches done, you could get a birdie or a tingle or a weird sensation where that was done.

00:02:00,070 --> 00:02:04,070
It's just scar formation.

00:02:04,070 --> 00:02:11,070
So, I don't want to raise too much concern, but you always want to, you know, suspect possibilities.

00:02:11,070 --> 00:02:17,070
What can you do for it? You wouldn't do, put anything out there that would increase replication.

00:02:17,070 --> 00:02:26,070
But I would certainly think some different herbal saves could be beneficial.

00:02:26,070 --> 00:02:32,070
I think coledula saves would be a good idea for that. I don't know that I would use company.

00:02:32,070 --> 00:02:46,070
I use coledula saves might be a good idea, even just some coconut oil could be good to go over scar over where you had radiation could be help.

00:02:46,070 --> 00:02:53,070
It could be healing and prevent further scar formation.

